    title "Instructions per mid bench 34.50 G -> 33.27 G (recorder fast path) -> 32.77 G (zero-width write skip), -16% since Phase 39; pinned wall p39 -> p41c mid 421/412/424 -> 398/409/409 ms, large 869/961 -> 840/899 ms (load 2.5-6); Phase 42 ceiling from the phase clock: the second anchor's plan is ~18 ms of ~400 ms, so batching two anchors saves at most ~12 ms (~3%) and is deferred"
    state verified
    result pass
    method observation
    observed_at git:e7c18f77a29d76236e83f446bbe6f81512aa03cf
    command "perf stat -e cpu_core/instructions/ -- taskset -c 0,2,4,6 ./jpxl-{p41,p41b,p41c} bench vardct-rate --input mid-photo.ppm --bpp 1 --lossy-preset balanced --iters 2 --threads 4; interleaved pinned p39 vs p41c with --diag on mid and large"
    summary """
        Writer store_ms on mid 35-38 -> 28-30 ms; count_ms 73-81 -> 56-83 ms (one pair contaminated by load). rate_plan_full for the second anchor plus finalist is plan_ms 37 (quantize 35), i.e. ~17 ms of quantization per plan; the anchor Count is unaffected by batching; a fixed bracket loses the first anchor's exact size as a predictor (second_anchor_rung uses it) and risks corrections at >= 60 ms each. Deferred rather than attempted, per docs/optimize.md's counters-before-mechanism rule; the user may override.
        """
}

