record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4h-lossy-reachable-2026-08-10/1 : evidence {
    title "At 65fe2e1 the harness completed all 24 cells (3 images x 4 rates x 2 codecs) with no encode or decode failure, so the lossy path is reachable from the CLI end to end. Every JPXL cell was encoded by jpxl encode --bpp, decoded by jpxl decode, and scored by jpxl compare against the source PPM; every cjxl cell was decoded by the oracle's own djxl. Rate targets are hit at low and mid rates: 0.4986/0.9946/1.9882 bpp against 0.5/1/2 at 0.8 MP, 0.4977/0.9947/1.9960 at 4 MP, 0.4991/0.9970 at 12 MP. Two cells undershoot because the quantizer ladder runs out of fine steps rather than because of any failure: 3.645 bpp against a 4.0 target at 4 MP, and 1.673 against 2.0 at 12 MP -- recorded as a finding in jpegxl-rs.observation.lossy-vardct-headsup-2026-08-10, not as a harness error. Spot check independent of the harness: jpxl encode --bpp 1.0 on the 0.8 MP image emitted 97,769 bytes against a 98,304-byte target and was accepted by both jpxl-decode and djxl v0.13.0."
