record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4i-metrics-correct-2026-08-10/1 : evidence {
    title "At d3950d7 the jpxl-conformance library suite with both perceptual features on is 51 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored -- 44 pre-4I plus seven gates. Identity: ssimulacra2_scores_an_identical_image_at_one_hundred pins an image against itself at exactly 100 (the metric's ceiling), butteraugli_scores_an_identical_image_at_zero pins both its distance and pnorm3 at ~0 (the opposite end of the scale). Direction: ssimulacra2_falls_as_distortion_rises and butteraugli_rises_as_distortion_rises pin the two opposite conventions separately, and the_two_perceptual_metrics_agree_on_which_image_is_worse cross-checks them against each other on the same pair -- if either wrapper had its sign convention inverted, that test fails. Preconditions: ssimulacra2_declines_shapes_it_cannot_score and butteraugli_declines_shapes_it_cannot_score pin None for a shape mismatch and for images below the 8x8 floor both metrics impose. Separately verified on real data: identical images score exactly 100.0000 / 0.0000, and across a 0.5-to-4 bpp sweep the scores move monotonically (ssimulacra2 23.85 -> 59.62 -> 80.01 -> 92.22; butteraugli 14.12 -> 6.64 -> 3.56 -> 1.17)."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:d3950d782182f5c688c73b2d563fa82bcde13419
    command "cargo test -p jpxl-conformance --lib --features perceptual"
    summary """
        At d3950d7 the jpxl-conformance library suite with both perceptual features on is 51 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored -- 44 pre-4I plus seven gates. Identity: ssimulacra2_scores_an_identical_image_at_one_hundred pins an image against itself at exactly 100 (the metric's ceiling), butteraugli_scores_an_identical_image_at_zero pins both its distance and pnorm3 at ~0 (the opposite end of the scale). Direction: ssimulacra2_falls_as_distortion_rises and butteraugli_rises_as_distortion_rises pin the two opposite conventions separately, and the_two_perceptual_metrics_agree_on_which_image_is_worse cross-checks them against each other on the same pair -- if either wrapper had its sign convention inverted, that test fails. Preconditions: ssimulacra2_declines_shapes_it_cannot_score and butteraugli_declines_shapes_it_cannot_score pin None for a shape mismatch and for images below the 8x8 floor both metrics impose. Separately verified on real data: identical images score exactly 100.0000 / 0.0000, and across a 0.5-to-4 bpp sweep the scores move monotonically (ssimulacra2 23.85 -> 59.62 -> 80.01 -> 92.22; butteraugli 14.12 -> 6.64 -> 3.56 -> 1.17).
        """
    author "GitHub Uploader"
}

record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4i-off-by-default-2026-08-10/1 : evidence {
    title "At d3950d7 the default build of jpxl-cli and jpxl-conformance is clippy-clean with no reference to either metric crate: both are optional dependencies gated behind the ssimulacra2 and butteraugli features, neither of which is in any default feature set, so a default cargo build --workspace does not fetch yuvxyb, thiserror, num-traits, imgref, rgb or archmage. Verified in both configurations: cargo fmt --check reports no diff in metrics.rs or main.rs, and cargo clippy reports nothing in either file with the features off or with --features jpxl-cli/perceptual on. The one lint the split surfaced -- an unused mut on the compare command's output line when neither perceptual block compiles -- is handled with a cfg_attr scoped to exactly that configuration rather than an unconditional allow."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:d3950d782182f5c688c73b2d563fa82bcde13419
    command "cargo clippy -p jpxl-cli -p jpxl-conformance --all-targets"
    summary """
        At d3950d7 the default build of jpxl-cli and jpxl-conformance is clippy-clean with no reference to either metric crate: both are optional dependencies gated behind the ssimulacra2 and butteraugli features, neither of which is in any default feature set, so a default cargo build --workspace does not fetch yuvxyb, thiserror, num-traits, imgref, rgb or archmage. Verified in both configurations: cargo fmt --check reports no diff in metrics.rs or main.rs, and cargo clippy reports nothing in either file with the features off or with --features jpxl-cli/perceptual on. The one lint the split surfaced -- an unused mut on the compare command's output line when neither perceptual block compiles -- is handled with a cfg_attr scoped to exactly that configuration rather than an unconditional allow.
        """
    author "GitHub Uploader"
}

record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4j-sweep-runs-2026-08-10/1 : evidence {
    title "At 5c6a138 the sweep completes all ten cells and reproduces the pre-commit run exactly, so the bit-allocation policy is now measurable end to end. Rows (bytes, ssimulacra2, butteraugli) at 0.8 MP / 2.0 bpp: shipped-default 195444, 80.0066, 3.5615; strength=0.0 196459, 81.9707, 3.1849; strength=0.10 196608, 79.7208, 3.8281; strength=0.40 195600, 79.7705, 3.5755; strength=0.60 195176, 79.6434, 3.5892; strength=1.00 196458, 79.8281, 3.5615; clamp=0.5 196045, 80.0022, 3.5488; clamp=2.0 196243, 79.6389, 3.4497; chroma=0.0 195384, 79.9275, 3.4474; chroma=1.0 195849, 79.8532, 3.5891. Every config encodes within 0.7% of the same size, so the comparison is at matched rate as intended. strength=0.0 produces a neutral field, which AqSetup treats exactly as AqMode::Off, and it is the best cell on both metrics -- the finding recorded in jpegxl-rs.observation.aq-field-is-a-net-perceptual-loss-2026-08-10."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:5c6a1381aa0de2cd592b91b2bf869d88677e07eb
    command "pwsh -NoProfile -File .agent/scratch/effort-ramp-2026-08-10/aq-sweep.ps1 small_0p8MP 2.0"
    summary """
        At 5c6a138 the sweep completes all ten cells and reproduces the pre-commit run exactly, so the bit-allocation policy is now measurable end to end. Rows (bytes, ssimulacra2, butteraugli) at 0.8 MP / 2.0 bpp: shipped-default 195444, 80.0066, 3.5615; strength=0.0 196459, 81.9707, 3.1849; strength=0.10 196608, 79.7208, 3.8281; strength=0.40 195600, 79.7705, 3.5755; strength=0.60 195176, 79.6434, 3.5892; strength=1.00 196458, 79.8281, 3.5615; clamp=0.5 196045, 80.0022, 3.5488; clamp=2.0 196243, 79.6389, 3.4497; chroma=0.0 195384, 79.9275, 3.4474; chroma=1.0 195849, 79.8532, 3.5891. Every config encodes within 0.7% of the same size, so the comparison is at matched rate as intended. strength=0.0 produces a neutral field, which AqSetup treats exactly as AqMode::Off, and it is the best cell on both metrics -- the finding recorded in jpegxl-rs.observation.aq-field-is-a-net-perceptual-loss-2026-08-10.
