record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4j-tuning-is-default-preserving-2026-08-10/1 : evidence {
    title "At 5c6a138 the jpxl-encode-policy library suite is 68 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored -- 65 pre-4J plus three gates. the_default_tuning_reproduces_the_hardcoded_field compares DesiredQuantField::from_atlas against from_atlas_tuned(AqTuning::default()) atom for atom across the whole grid in both AQ directions, so turning the constants into data provably did not move any existing lossy output. a_stronger_tuning_spreads_the_field_further pins that the strength knob widens the field's range, measured with the clamp opened so it isolates strength (at the shipped clamp this fixture's flat/noise contrast saturates, which would have made the comparison vacuous), and that zero strength yields a neutral field. tuning_is_sanitised_into_the_representable_range pins that a negative strength clamps to zero, an absurd clamp caps at two octaves, and a NaN chroma weight falls back to the default rather than poisoning the field."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:5c6a1381aa0de2cd592b91b2bf869d88677e07eb
    command "cargo test -p jpxl-encode-policy --lib"
    summary """
        At 5c6a138 the jpxl-encode-policy library suite is 68 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored -- 65 pre-4J plus three gates. the_default_tuning_reproduces_the_hardcoded_field compares DesiredQuantField::from_atlas against from_atlas_tuned(AqTuning::default()) atom for atom across the whole grid in both AQ directions, so turning the constants into data provably did not move any existing lossy output. a_stronger_tuning_spreads_the_field_further pins that the strength knob widens the field's range, measured with the clamp opened so it isolates strength (at the shipped clamp this fixture's flat/noise contrast saturates, which would have made the comparison vacuous), and that zero strength yields a neutral field. tuning_is_sanitised_into_the_representable_range pins that a negative strength clamps to zero, an absurd clamp caps at two octaves, and a NaN chroma weight falls back to the default rather than poisoning the field.
        """
    author "GitHub Uploader"
}

record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4k-contracts-hold-2026-08-10/1 : evidence {
    title "At 586bb19 the jpxl-encode-policy library suite is 72 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored -- 68 pre-4K plus four gates. The pre-existing contracts pass UNMODIFIED: the_loop_lands_under_a_target_and_close_to_it (never over, within slack, inside the price cap), the_loop_survives_a_non_monotone_pocket (returns the best it priced AND the brute-forced global optimum on a 2000-rung sawtooth), the_fill_recovers_a_notch_hidden_behind_an_infeasible_one, the_price_budget_is_a_hard_cap, a_target_above_the_ceiling_saturates_at_the_finest_rung, a_target_below_the_floor_is_refused_with_the_floor_in_the_error. New: an_aimed_probe_that_lands_in_a_spike_does_not_fence_off_the_rungs_above_it puts a narrow infeasible spike exactly where false position aims, with the true optimum above it, and asserts the loop still returns the brute-forced optimum -- this is the direct proof of the safety rule that an aimed probe never becomes the new hi. an_aimed_step_targets_the_crossing_not_the_middle and an_aimed_step_declines_what_it_cannot_aim_at pin the stepping function itself. aimed_stepping_reaches_the_target_in_fewer_prices pins that targets in the global_scale segment land within tolerance in at most 16 prices. Integration: rate_loop 11 passed 1 ignored, vardct_roundtrip 12 passed, boundary 2 passed; vardct_oracle 9/10 with the pre-existing both_oracles_decode_a_stream_from_the_hf_mul_segment failure, verified earlier this session to fail identically at clean HEAD."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:586bb1901f94605d4bc5e018169a6dcb30402594
    command "cargo test -p jpxl-encode-policy --lib"
    summary """
        At 586bb19 the jpxl-encode-policy library suite is 72 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored -- 68 pre-4K plus four gates. The pre-existing contracts pass UNMODIFIED: the_loop_lands_under_a_target_and_close_to_it (never over, within slack, inside the price cap), the_loop_survives_a_non_monotone_pocket (returns the best it priced AND the brute-forced global optimum on a 2000-rung sawtooth), the_fill_recovers_a_notch_hidden_behind_an_infeasible_one, the_price_budget_is_a_hard_cap, a_target_above_the_ceiling_saturates_at_the_finest_rung, a_target_below_the_floor_is_refused_with_the_floor_in_the_error. New: an_aimed_probe_that_lands_in_a_spike_does_not_fence_off_the_rungs_above_it puts a narrow infeasible spike exactly where false position aims, with the true optimum above it, and asserts the loop still returns the brute-forced optimum -- this is the direct proof of the safety rule that an aimed probe never becomes the new hi. an_aimed_step_targets_the_crossing_not_the_middle and an_aimed_step_declines_what_it_cannot_aim_at pin the stepping function itself. aimed_stepping_reaches_the_target_in_fewer_prices pins that targets in the global_scale segment land within tolerance in at most 16 prices. Integration: rate_loop 11 passed 1 ignored, vardct_roundtrip 12 passed, boundary 2 passed; vardct_oracle 9/10 with the pre-existing both_oracles_decode_a_stream_from_the_hf_mul_segment failure, verified earlier this session to fail identically at clean HEAD.
        """
    author "GitHub Uploader"
}

record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4k-fewer-full-encodes-2026-08-10/1 : evidence {
    title "At 586bb19, measured against the entry-4 baseline on the same host and corpus. 4 MP: 1 bpp 92.2 s -> 19.8 s (4.7x), and rate accuracy improves too -- 537,114 -> 539,797 bytes against a 540,000 target, i.e. 0.5% short becomes 0.04% short; 2 bpp 98.4 s -> 55.3 s (1.8x); 4 bpp 241.6 s -> 145.4 s (1.66x). 12 MP: 1 bpp 200.1 s -> 54.3 s (3.7x) at essentially identical bytes (1,495,450 -> 1,494,376); 2 bpp 559.3 s -> 336.5 s (1.66x). REGRESSION, recorded rather than omitted: the two cases that already missed their target miss it by about one percentage point more (4 MP 4 bpp 8.9% -> 9.5% short; 12 MP 2 bpp 16.3% -> 17.6%), because the abandoned aiming bet costs one probe and those cases have none to spare. Root cause of the undershoot is unchanged and unaddressed: every failing case still reports 24 fast prices, the Fast ladder's cap, so the remaining lever is the fast/full budget split or a cheaper Fast price, not further stepping work."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:586bb1901f94605d4bc5e018169a6dcb30402594
    command "jpxl encode <corpus>.ppm out.jxl --bpp N"
    summary """
        At 586bb19, measured against the entry-4 baseline on the same host and corpus. 4 MP: 1 bpp 92.2 s -> 19.8 s (4.7x), and rate accuracy improves too -- 537,114 -> 539,797 bytes against a 540,000 target, i.e. 0.5% short becomes 0.04% short; 2 bpp 98.4 s -> 55.3 s (1.8x); 4 bpp 241.6 s -> 145.4 s (1.66x). 12 MP: 1 bpp 200.1 s -> 54.3 s (3.7x) at essentially identical bytes (1,495,450 -> 1,494,376); 2 bpp 559.3 s -> 336.5 s (1.66x). REGRESSION, recorded rather than omitted: the two cases that already missed their target miss it by about one percentage point more (4 MP 4 bpp 8.9% -> 9.5% short; 12 MP 2 bpp 16.3% -> 17.6%), because the abandoned aiming bet costs one probe and those cases have none to spare. Root cause of the undershoot is unchanged and unaddressed: every failing case still reports 24 fast prices, the Fast ladder's cap, so the remaining lever is the fast/full budget split or a cheaper Fast price, not further stepping work.
        """
    author "GitHub Uploader"
}

