record jpegxl-rs.evidence.pqc-pr2-reference-parity-2026-08-22/1 : evidence {
    title "Against the rust-av ssimulacra2 0.5.1 crate: six photograph pairs (1024x768 crops of mid.ppm and source.ppm, noise/blur/quantisation) differ by at most 0.03; the size-drift probe on mid.ppm differs 0.03 at 0.27 MP, 0.09 at 1.1 MP and 0.18 at 4.3 MP (score ~82); synthetic flat-heavy content at score ~93 differs +0.14 at 256x192 up to +1.07 at 1024x768 because the oracle's f32 blur recursion ripple inflates its rectified edge maps while this crate's f64 recursion does not; identical images score exactly 100, monotone in distortion, colour conversion matches to 1e-6 and the blur to 6e-6. The tolerances pin that envelope."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:23635f689884489cfb720d65b49afce1901381c6
    command "cd JPXL && cargo test -p jpxl-perceptual --release --features parity-oracle --test parity -- --nocapture"
    artifact "JPXL/crates/jpxl-perceptual/tests/parity.rs"
    summary """
        Against the rust-av ssimulacra2 0.5.1 crate: six photograph pairs (1024x768 crops of mid.ppm and source.ppm, noise/blur/quantisation) differ by at most 0.03; the size-drift probe on mid.ppm differs 0.03 at 0.27 MP, 0.09 at 1.1 MP and 0.18 at 4.3 MP (score ~82); synthetic flat-heavy content at score ~93 differs +0.14 at 256x192 up to +1.07 at 1024x768 because the oracle's f32 blur recursion ripple inflates its rectified edge maps while this crate's f64 recursion does not; identical images score exactly 100, monotone in distortion, colour conversion matches to 1e-6 and the blur to 6e-6. The tolerances pin that envelope.
        """
}

