    command "python3 .agent/scratch/n0-ladder-extract-20260829/identity_n0.py; python3 .agent/scratch/r1-render-scratch-20260829/wall_ab_r1.py"
    artifact ".agent/scratch/r1-render-scratch-20260829/wall-ab-final.log"
    summary """
        R1 (a9d421c + 8f3192e) is exact and measured: 16/16 cells byte-identical vs the e895c32 baseline CLI (both quality efforts and the rate path), and every A/B run's output byte-identical run for run. Quiet-host interleaved A/B vs pre-R1 c41a705, --threads 4: 4.3 MP quality wall 1.121 s to 1.097 s (-2.2%), max RSS 1059 MiB to 1011 MiB (-48 MiB); 12 MP quality wall 2.939 s to 2.974 s (+1.2%), max RSS 2008 MiB to 2022 MiB, under the 2 GiB ceiling. The 12 MP residual is attributed: ~30 ms/encode is release_scratch's serial munmaps of the ~900 MB frame scratch each probe, kept because retaining the scratch across probes measured 2284 MiB peak, over the ceiling; render-stage timings themselves are equal to baseline. 1605 tests, clippy -D warnings, fmt --check green.
        """
}

